      "yield": "6-8 servings",
      "tips": "",
      "ingredients": "For the Cake:\n1 ½ cups all-purpose flour\n¾ cup unsweetened cocoa powder\n1 ½ tsp. baking powder\n1 ½ tsp. baking soda\n1 tsp. salt  \n1 cup granulated sugar\n1/2 cup vegetable oil\n1 cup buttermilk\n1 tsp. vanilla extract\n1 cup hot coffee (brewed)\n1/2 cup Toblerone Crunchy Almond Chocolate, chopped\nFor the Tres Leches Mixture:\n1 cup  sweetened condensed milk\n1 cup  evaporated milk\n1 cup whole chocolate milk\n1 tsp. vanilla extract\nFor the Toblerone Topping:\n¼ cup heavy cream\n1 ½ cup Toblerone Crunchy Almond Chocolate, chopped\n1 cup whipped cream",
      "procedure": "Preheat oven to 175°C. Grease and flour a 9x13 inch baking pan.\n\nIn a large bowl, whisk together flour, cocoa powder, baking powder, baking soda, and salt.\n\nIn a separate bowl, whisk together sugar, oil, buttermilk, vanilla extract, and hot coffee.\n\nGradually add the wet ingredients to the dry ingredients, mixing until just combined. Be careful not to overmix. Stir in chopped Toblerone Chocolate.\n\nPour batter into the prepared pan and bake for 25-30 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.\n\nLet the cake cool in the pan for 10 minutes before inverting it onto a wire rack to cool completely.  \n\nIn a bowl, whisk together sweetened condensed milk, evaporated milk, whole chocolate milk, and vanilla extract.\n\nOnce the cake is completely cool, poke holes all over the top using a fork.\n\nSlowly pour the Tres Leches mixture evenly over the cake, allowing it to soak in completely.\n\nCover the cake with plastic wrap and refrigerate for at least 4 hours, or overnight.\n\nIn a small saucepan, heat the heavy cream over medium heat until it simmers.\n\nPlace half cup Toblerone Chocolate in a heatproof bowl. Pour the hot cream over the chocolate. Let the mixture stand for a few minutes to allow the chocolate to melt. Then, gently stir until smooth and creamy.\n\nCombine ganache and whipped cream. \n\nCut the cake into squares and top with prepared chocolate whipped cream and the remaining chopped Toblerone Chocolate."
